@ 10.1.2.8 - Proto-Philippine to Kankanay
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Llamzon, Teodoro A. (1975), “Proto-Philippine Phonology”. Archipel 9(1):29 – 42; and from other changes and information from this document *R seems to have had a few different reflexes, mainly one of /l ɡ j/; if /ɡ j/ occurred, /ɡ/ was more probable at word boundaries and /j/ was more probable medially Something seems to have changed to əw finally but the paper may have an error here
	{*P:[+voice],*:[+continuant]} > d
	{z,*j} > d / V_V
	*j > ɡ / _#
	c > s
	{h,q} > ∅
	iw > uj